WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.336
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy Award-winning actress

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.804
and comedian who you know
from her work on

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:08.741
"SNL," "Bridesmaids," and
the Netflix series "Big Mouth."

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:12.011
She stars in and
executive-produces "Loot,"

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:13.880
which premieres
on Apple TV+ tomorrow.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.082
Please welcome back to the show
our good friend

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.984
Maya Rudolph, everybody!

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.887
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:43.208 --> 00:00:47.546
Maya! How are you?
-Hiya, Maya.

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:50.149
-It's so nice to see you.
-It's nice to see you, Sethly.

00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:51.351
-I know.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:52.519
I know we've talked about it
before,

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.720
but when you started at "SNL,"
everybody --

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.656
a lot of the women on the cast
called you "Mayers."

00:00:57.656 --> 00:00:59.092
-Yes.
-Like, "Mayers!"

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.261
Which is my last name,
and I thought it was very rude.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.828
-Yeah. I mean,
I did have seniority,

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:04.063
so I feel like it's okay.

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.431
-You did have seniority.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.500
I should have legally changed
my last name.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.902
-I think you should have.
It was a sign.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.470
-How are you?
-I'm great. How are you?

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.639
-I'm good.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:15.708
Last time you were here,
we were talking about

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.310
your four beautiful children

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.446
and how much they were engaging
with your work.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:21.881
Have they seen more
of your work?

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:25.050
Are they more familiar
with your output at this point?

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.087
-I mean, I still
don't think anyone wants to

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:32.158
watch "Big Mouth" because of me.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.593
-Okay, gotcha.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:37.897
-Because I think it's gross to
hear your mom talk about boners.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:42.168
-Yeah. I think that's, like,
that's age-old.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.803
-That's a boner deterrent.
-Yeah.

00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:47.106
-I was like, "I know how
I won't get my kids

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.475
to think about boners.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.012
I'll be a hormone monstress."

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:56.182
Yeah, so they don't --
-Do they watch old "SNLs"?

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.282
-They do, actually.
-Okay, that's good.

00:01:57.282 --> 00:01:58.684
-Actually, you know what?

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.286
What was the one
that I just showed

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.288
Pearl the other day?

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.657
It was --
I think she was shocked.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.527
It was, like, a true early-2000s
host, like, "Wait.

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:09.762
You knew that person?"

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.598
I was like, "Yeah.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:18.471
Yeah, I was alive in 2002.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.139
It was pretty cool."

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:23.208
-I've had it backfire on me
with my kids where, like,

00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:25.245
my kids met Wiig, Kristen Wiig.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.646
-Yeah.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.981
-You knew which one I was
talking about.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:32.017
-I was getting her confused
with the Cleveland Wiig we know.

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:34.486
There's so many Wiigs.

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:36.756
-With the double I's.
They're all, yeah, that, too.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.092
That very common spelling,
with two I's next to each other.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.627
But she played --
They met her and they liked her.

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:43.062
And I was like,
"Oh, you have to watch this."

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.198
And she played, like, a
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:47.766
float that was, like,
really scary.

00:02:47.766 --> 00:02:48.968
And I showed it to them,
and then they were like,

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.002
"We don't want to
see her anymore."

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.170
-They were like --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.571
-"We don't wanna see that lady.

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:54.740
Yeah, we didn't realize
what a bad vibe she was."

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.575
-"That's your friend?"
-Yeah.

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:58.478
-"Great friends, dad."

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:02.582
-Are your kids as musically
talented as you are?

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:06.552
-I think they have the gift
of music and they don't realize

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:10.022
how great they are, so they kind
of keep it to themselves.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.425
But, yes,
I force them all to play,

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:13.959
to have, like, piano lessons.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.629
-Do you want them --
-To start a band?

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.365
Yeah.
-Okay. Would that be the dream?

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:22.068
-Well, I have four kids, so,
like, during COVID, I was like,

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.303
"Guys, it would be great if
you played those drums."

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:26.372
Or like, "I mean,
there's a piano, a bass,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.440
a guitar, and an amp in here.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.675
Who knew?"

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.644
-Do you think you'd be
a really good band mom?

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:34.213
Would you be, like, in the wings
watching your family?

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:35.448
-I'd probably be like --
What's that

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.116
Goldie Hawn-Susan Sarandon
movie?

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.986
I'd be like --
-Oh, gosh, I don't know.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.055
-They're both
wearing leather jackets

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.856
and, like, ripped T-shirts,

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.924
but they're like
in their late 40s.

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:47.526
They're like...

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:50.029
I'd be embarrassing.
-Oh, that's good.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.631
Well, then
I also want it to happen.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:54.366
-I would really like that,
just to be, like, a groupie.

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:56.302
Like, "Those are my kids!

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.737
They rock!"

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:01.274
Just, like, no bra.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:06.178
-They're like, "Wait. Your mom
is the one without a bra

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:07.847
and the hormone monster?"

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:11.884
-"Your mom hit on me at
craft services."

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:17.457
-They -- Now, all your kids
were in "Licorice Pizza."

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:18.757
-Yeah.
-As were you.

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:19.925
-My husband's movie.
-How was that?

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:22.929
-That was actually
a magical thing,

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:26.566
because COVID happened,
lockdown happened,

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:30.469
and then Paul was told like,
"Okay, you can shoot now."

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.438
But my kids were not allowed
to go back to school.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.672
So we were doing Zoom school.

00:04:33.672 --> 00:04:35.774
And it was a scary time,
and no one was vaccinated.

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:40.646
And it provided this amazing
experience where my kids,

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:43.316
their friends,
their friends' parents,

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:47.653
my parents, my nanny --
we were all in it,

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:48.821
and so we were all around.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.356
And so we had, like,
a little world.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.692
Like, we were living
in the 1970s

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.627
in the San Fernando Valley
for like three months.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.295
It was beautiful.
-That's great.

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:59.932
How did they take to
being directed by their father?

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.201
-I think it's helped.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:04.036
-Oh!
-No, no. They loved it.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:07.373
Like, it only made their worship
of their father stronger.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.507
-Oh, that's really cool.

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:11.244
-They just think
he's such a stud and a cool guy.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.045
-You also filmed "Disenchanted."

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:15.281
-Yes.
-This is you and Amy Adams.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:17.083
You seem to be --
There seemed to be, like,

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.686
a slightly eviler vibe
to what you're doing here.

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:23.322
-Yeah. This is like the meat and
potatoes of character actors.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:26.258
Like, you want to be the evil
villain in a Disney movie.

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:28.627
It's, like,
everything you could possibly --

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:29.728
It's drag.

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:31.230
I'm doing drag.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.933
And it was so fun.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.100
It was so much fun.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.071
I had long nails
and I got to be nasty

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.472
and I got to
sing and dance and wear

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:43.075
really tight corsets
and beautiful gowns.

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:46.712
And Amy Adams is --
-So lovely.

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.281
-She's the greatest.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:51.184
Plus, she's already
a magical human being,

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:54.520
and then, as Giselle,
it was like it was real,

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.056
like it was
a true princess come to life.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.658
But it was so funny,
because, like, everything

00:05:59.658 --> 00:06:00.926
about her is so beautiful.

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:04.229
It's like hanging out
with Cinderella.

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:06.865
And so everything about her
was, like, this beautiful

00:06:06.865 --> 00:06:09.969
white carriage and her horses,
and they were so lovely.

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:11.537
And I realized
I had a carriage, too.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:12.805
I had a black carriage.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:16.408
And I had these big, beefy,
like, black horses.

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:18.276
And her horses --

00:06:18.276 --> 00:06:20.145
My horses peed a lot.

00:06:20.145 --> 00:06:22.215
-Yeah.
-And her horses never peed.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:24.717
And we realized,
"Oh, those are female horses."

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:26.552
Mine were male.
-Uh-huh.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:31.323
-They had the biggest [bleep]
I've ever seen.

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:35.528
And at one point,

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:36.762
I have to get out of
the carriage

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:37.896
and talk to her and greet her.

00:06:37.896 --> 00:06:41.299
And she goes
to curtsy in front of me,

00:06:41.299 --> 00:06:44.937
and it sounded like someone
threw a bucket of water

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.338
on the ground.

00:06:46.338 --> 00:06:48.407
And I tried not to look,
because it was right behind me.

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:50.076
And it was going on for a while.

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:51.944
I'm like,
"How many buckets are they --

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:53.645
Don't they know we're rolling?"

00:06:53.645 --> 00:06:55.548
And we kept going,
and then I looked back

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:58.517
and I saw some people doing
like, kind of church laughing.

00:06:58.517 --> 00:07:00.786
They're, like, facing me.

00:07:00.786 --> 00:07:03.689
The horse was still pissing.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:06.558
It peed for so long.

00:07:06.558 --> 00:07:07.727
Have you ever seen a horse pee?

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:09.195
-I don't think
at this level, no.

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:12.531
-Wow! Maybe it's because
it was an Irish horse.

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:15.033
It was very healthy.
-Yeah, very healthy.

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:16.668
I hope they keep that in.

00:07:16.668 --> 00:07:19.372
-I think they will.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:23.008
It sounds like
a Disney thing, right?

00:07:23.008 --> 00:07:24.510
-We'll be right back with more

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.212
from Maya Rudolph, everybody!

